Fix build of the NVIDIA open GPU kernel modules against Linux 7.x.

__to_hwgpio() declares its gdev parameter const, but gpio_device_get_chip()
takes a non-const struct gpio_device *. Clang rejects this under -Werror with
-Wincompatible-pointer-types-discards-qualifiers, breaking the build:

  ././common/inc/nv-linux.h:1737:51: error: passing 'const struct gpio_device *'
  to parameter of type 'struct gpio_device *' discards qualifiers

gpio_device_get_chip() does not mutate gdev, so casting away const at the call
site is safe. Upstream issue: https://github.com/xddxdd/nix-cachyos-kernel/issues/101

--- a/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h
+++ b/kernel-open/common/inc/nv-linux.h
@@ -1734,7 +1734,7 @@
      * port and pin in args[0] and of_xlate sums per-port pin counts
      * to produce the real offset.
      */
-    struct gpio_chip *chip = gpio_device_get_chip(gdev);
+    struct gpio_chip *chip = gpio_device_get_chip((struct gpio_device *)gdev);
 
     if (chip->of_xlate)
         return chip->of_xlate(chip, gpiospec, NULL);
